+   Two distinct float comparators are characterized for the Arm 1 served NLL ($2.568047$ nats):
+   - **Own-QAT Representation Gap (within adapted artifact):** relative to its own unquantized float weights ($2.564809$ nats), the quantization representation penalty is $\mathbf{+0.003238\text{ nats}}$ ($\approx +0.0032$ nats), directly isolating the quantization loss within the adapted model with a $9\times$ margin under the $\le 0.0300$ nats gate.
+   - **Matched-Control Difference (vs separate Arm 2 float control):** relative to the unquantized float control trained without QAT ($2.564863$ nats), the difference is $\mathbf{+0.003184\text{ nats}}$ ($\approx +0.0032$ nats).
+   Both differences round to $+0.0032$ nats, but only the former isolates representation loss within the adapted artifact.
+   Against the pre-registered baseline target bounds:
+   - Literal pre-registration target: $\le 2.5255$ nats (based on cited parent $2.4955 + 0.0300$ nats from PR #1470 pre-registration; local receipt UNAVAILABLE).
